{
 "about": "Ch2 Deep Cache level layout v2 (designer, 2026-10-14; v1 2026-10-13, approved by Julius). Source of truth for the world, the map (screen layer) and the engineer. How to read every block: `notes`. Island models: ch2-island-{s,m,l}.glb, origin = top centre, walkable y = 0 inside `models[m].outline`. After editing, run: python3 3d/ch2/mklayout.py",
 "version": 2,
 "notes": {
  "units": "Metres, seconds. x = east, z = south (down on the map), y = up. Angles in radians unless the key ends in Deg.",
  "islands": "Model s/m/l from `models`, placed with scale (number or [sx,sy,sz]) then rotY (three.js Object3D.rotation.y), then pos. Walkable top = pos.y. Collider = models[m].outline (model units, [x,z]) scaled in x/z, pulled in to 96 % (so you don't stand on the rim lip), rotated by rotY, moved to pos. `slab` = solid deck thickness under the top, `depth` = how far the crystal underside hangs below that (looks only, never collide with it).",
  "ring": "An island with `ring` expands into `count` islands `<id>-<k>`, k = 0..count-1: angle a = (startDeg + k*360/count) deg, pos = centre + radius*(cos a, 0, sin a), y = centre.y + (k odd ? +yJitter : -yJitter)*0.6, rotY = k*1.3.",
  "bridges": "A ribbon `width` m wide along `points`, walkable on its centre line. `curve: true` = three.js CatmullRomCurve3(points, false, \"centripetal\"), sampled with getSpacedPoints(ceil(length/1 m)); same library, so sample it yourself and you get identical points. Otherwise a straight polyline with exact corners.",
  "oldBoard": "Column top = disc of top.radius at top.y. Slabs: a slab with `pos` uses it and rotY; otherwise a = spiralDeg in rad, pos = column.pos + spiralRadius*(cos a, 0, sin a) with y = slab.y, rotY = -a + PI/2. Walkable box size[0] x size[1] (x = long side), top at its y. Drift: offset = drift * sin(2*PI*t/period + phase), moved along the slab's local x = (cos rotY, 0, -sin rotY). Carry the player by the slab's per-frame delta.",
  "lifts": "Box size[0] x size[1] at pos (bottom). k = 0.5 - 0.5*cos(2*PI*t/period); y = lerp(pos.y, yTop, clamp(k*1.25 - 0.125, 0, 1)), so it waits a moment at both ends. Carries the player.",
  "clouds": "Sphere of radius r at pos + drift * sin(2*PI*t/period). Inside = token drain (script: -1 per second).",
  "tilt": "tilt: true = tilts whenever stood on; tilt: \"round3\" = only from forge round 3 (static before). Target tilt = (dz/R, -dx/R) * physics.tilt.max around x/z, where dx,dz = player offset from the island centre and R = model radius * max(scale x,z); eased at tilt.rate per second; the island sinks physics.tilt.sink m while occupied (eased at sinkRate).",
  "waves": "Reset waves = red laser scan lines (look still in review with Julius; this data holds for both takes). Station on bridge `bridge`, straight segment `segment` (points[segment] -> points[segment+1]), at fraction t. The line lies across the bridge (length = bridge width + 1 m) and moves ALONG the segment: cycle c = floor((time+offset)/period), ph = (time+offset) - c*period; while ph < sweep it is on, at along = s*(-span + 2*span*ph/sweep), s = +1 for even c, -1 for odd c (it runs back the next time); after that it is off and waits at along = s*span until the period ends. Height follows the segment slope. Hit: on, |along_player - along| < 0.35, |lateral| < width/2 + 0.3, 0 < player.y - line.y + 1 < 4. Dashing passes through. Telegraph: in the last 1.2 s of the rest the emitter charges and a dotted red line marks where the next pass starts.",
  "tokens": "tokens.spots = ground points; the orb floats `hover` above, taken within `radius`, +`value` tokens.",
  "crates": "pickups kind 'crate' = the player's Ch1 installs at fixed spots by label; crateSpares = free spots for installs without a spot (e.g. decoy packages). Crates are 1.1 m cubes on the floor, walkable on top.",
  "forge": "Dais tiers: within r of the centre the floor is pos.y + y (3.5 -> +0.9, 4.8 -> +0.5). Four slot pylons (footprint size[0] x size[2], 2 m tall) at radius 3 and angles 45/135/225/315 deg, input order = slots; slotPos = the glowing frame centre for E and the item flying in.",
  "forgeFight": "Round 1: flood bits enter from bitSpawns (2 m above the island, between the edge platforms). Round 2: plus waveLanes, the same red scan lines as the Reset Run but across the forge island: the line lies perpendicular to dir, `length` long, centre moves along dir over +-span with the waves timing. Round 3: plus clouds (same motion as hazards.clouds) and the edge islands with tilt \"round3\" start tilting.",
  "physics": "walk m/s; gravity m/s2; jump = launch speed m/s; glideFall = max fall speed while Space is held and falling; dash = dashSpeed m/s flat for dashTime s, then dashCooldown; hover = orb centre above the feet; voidY = fall line -> respawn at the last pad. Horizontal velocity eases to the input at groundAccel (1/s) on the ground, airAccel in the air. coyote = s you can still jump after leaving an edge. stepUp = how far above the feet a surface still catches you; snapDown = how far you stick to a surface going down while walking. padRadius = touch radius of a respawn pad (and |dy| < 1)."
 },
